      ⍝ dyadic A→B with nonzero A, evaluated via ⍎ from inside a defined
      ⍝ function: A is relative to the line CONTAINING the ⍎ call (line
      ⍝ 2 here), exactly as if A→B had been written directly on that
      ⍝ line -- found by walking up the )SI to the nearest enclosing
      ⍝ real function (this used to be an unconditional SYNTAX ERROR,
      ⍝ and, before that, silently computed the wrong target line)
      ⍝
      )ERASE FOO
∇FOO
