      FOO
DOMAIN ERROR+
      100→1
      ^  ^

      ⍝ dyadic A→B with nonzero A, jumping between ⋄-separated
      ⍝ statements inside a lambda: also a clean DOMAIN ERROR (a
      ⍝ lambda has no real multi-line structure of its own for a
      ⍝ cross-statement jump to land in -- this used to crash the
      ⍝ interpreter outright instead of erroring)
      ⍝
      )SIC
      { ⎕←⎕LC ⋄ 2→1 ⋄ ⎕←⎕LC }
1
DOMAIN ERROR+
λ1[1]  2→1
       ^^

      ⍝ same two ⍎ A→B cases again, but at top-level immediate
      ⍝ execution (no enclosing function at all) -- A=0 still works,
      ⍝ nonzero A is still a SYNTAX ERROR
      ⍝
      )SIC
      N←3
      ⍎'0→0<N←⎕←N-1'
2
1
0
      ⍎'2→1'
SYNTAX ERROR+
      2→1
      ^ ^

      ⍝ Bugs28 #13 regression: a branch introduced into a lambda at run
      ⍝ time by ⍎ (impossible to write literally -- {→0} is rejected at
      ⍝ fix time already) used to end the whole session -- either an
      ⍝ internal "should never be called" reduce/FIXME, or a dangling
      ⍝ TOK_SI_PUSHED left in the caller once the lambda's own )SI level
      ⍝ was popped without ever supplying it a result. Both are now a
      ⍝ clean VALUE ERROR (the lambda has no result), the same as the
      ⍝ statement gives in immediate execution (Bugs37 #46), and the
      ⍝ session stays usable.
      ⍝
      ⎕EC '{⍎''→0''}1'
 0  3 1  VALUE ERROR+                                        
               {⍎'→0'}1                                      
                ^                                            
         No assignment to result variable Z in e.g. ∇Z←... ? 

      ⎕EC '{⍎''→2''}1'
 0  3 1  VALUE ERROR+                                        
               {⍎'→2'}1                                      
                ^                                            
         No assignment to result variable Z in e.g. ∇Z←... ? 

      ⎕FX 'Z←FBR B' 'Z←⍎''→0'''
FBR

      FBR 1

      ⍝ the )SI stays usable afterward
      ⍝
      )ERASE FBR

      )SIC
      )ERASE FOO
      )ERASE N
      )ERASE X
      )CHECK BRIEF

